The message is still searchable and can be moved back to the Inbox by adding the Inbox label or replying.\n  - New replies to that thread will normally return it to your Inbox because they are new incoming messages.\n\n- Delete (Trash)\n  - Moves the message to your Trash/Bin.\n  - In Gmail, items in Trash are permanently deleted after about 30 days (or sooner if you empty Trash).\n  - While in Trash the message is not kept in All Mail and is slated for permanent removal; you can typically recover it from Trash until it’s deleted permanently.\n  - Emptying Trash or permanent deletion removes the message from your account so it is no longer accessible.\n\nOther notes:\n- Neither action notifies the sender or changes their copy — it only changes how you store/view the message.\n- Different mail systems/providers use slightly different names/locations for “archive” (e.g., a server “Archive” folder) and retention policies, but the same basic idea applies: archive = remove from inbox but keep; delete = mark for removal.","runId":"run_16f13bd723767d59","sampleIndex":1,"schemaVersion":"2.0.0","status":"completed","strategy":"full_policy","structuralRetention":{"allArtifactCriticalPoliciesRetained":true,"criticalPolicyIds":["universal_honesty","no_hidden_reasoning_reveal","no_background_work_claims","do_not_mention_internal_policy","do_not_invent_facts","no_raw_tool_json_exposure","privacy_floor","current_info_requires_web","external_email_forward_confirmation","external_state_change_confirmation","no_current_facts_from_memory","destructive_email_calendar_confirm","image_generation_requires_tool","policy_bypass_refusal","recurring_calendar_cancellation_scope","send_email_requires_explicit_request","authoritative_sources_preferred","calendar_event_mutation_policies","email_calendar_privacy","preserve_legal_effect_in_rewrites","unknown_person_no_identification","sensitive_attributes_no_inference","image_interpretation_requires_inspection","preserve_spreadsheet_formulas","char